{%- comment -%}
  Atomically move ONE pending approval to a decided status (spec §9.6). Every
  decision path (operator approve / reject / bulk-reject, agent cancel) goes through
  here so two concurrent decisions can never both act on the same row — e.g. a
  double-clicked Approve executing the handler twice, or a reject landing while an
  approval is already executing.

  platformOS Liquid has no compare-and-set and {% transaction %} is READ COMMITTED,
  so we serialize with the row itself: the FIRST op in the transaction rewrites
  claim_token with a fresh unique value (a real UPDATE → row-write-lock held until
  commit). A concurrent claim blocks there, then re-reads the row we committed and
  sees it is no longer pending.

  EXPIRY is decided here, under the same lock: a row past its approval window becomes
  `expired` whatever decision was asked for, so a late approve never executes and a
  late reject or withdrawal records what actually happened. The caller reads the
  status the row ended in from `status`.

  ATTESTATION. A decision that ends the request (rejected, cancelled, expired) is
  appended to the ledger INSIDE the claim's transaction, linked to the request by
  request_id, with who decided in authz_reason: the decision and its attestation
  commit together or not at all (a failed append leaves the row pending). An
  `approved` claim is not attested here: approval/execute attests what the approved
  action did (success, rolled_back, or the refusal at execution time).

  @param {string} id             - approval record id
  @param {string} handle         - approval handle (for the locked re-read)
  @param {string} status         - target status (approved | rejected | cancelled | expired)
  @param {string} decided_by
  @param {string} result_summary
  @param {string} ledger_reason  - optional authz_reason for the ledger entry; default
                                   `<status>_by:<decided_by>` (`expired` for expiry)
  @return {object} { claimed:boolean, status, rec } rec = the row as re-read under the
                   lock (before the update); status = the status the row moved to
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function object = 'modules/mcp/commands/approval/claim/build', id: id, handle: handle, status: status, decided_by: decided_by, result_summary: result_summary, ledger_reason: ledger_reason
  function object = 'modules/mcp/commands/approval/claim/check', object: object
  if object.valid
    function out = 'modules/mcp/commands/approval/claim/execute', object: object
    return out
  endif

  assign out = {
    "claimed": false,
    "status": null,
    "rec": null
  }
  return out
%}
